<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title><%= vuln.name %> - Vuln-World</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #fff; color: #333; line-height: 1.6; }
    header { background: #111; color: #fff; padding: 20px; }
    header a { color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; }
    .container { max-width: 800px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 0 20px; }
    .btn { display: inline-block; padding: 10px 20px; background: #0056b3; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 4px; margin: 10px 0; }
    .diagram { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 20px; font-family: monospace; white-space: pre; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #ccc; overflow-x: auto; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <a href="/vulnerabilities">← Back to Catalog</a>
  </header>
  <div class="container">
    <h1><%= vuln.name %></h1>
    <p><strong>Category:</strong> <%= vuln.category %> | <strong>Difficulty:</strong> <%= vuln.difficulty %></p>
    
    <h2>1. What Is It?</h2>
    <p>An explanation of <%= vuln.name %> goes here.</p>
    
    <h2>2. Visual Explanation</h2>
    <div class="diagram">Browser
   │
   │ Request
   ▼
Server
   │
   │ Vulnerable logic
   ▼
Database</div>

    <h2>3. Try The Lab</h2>
    <a href="/labs/<%= vuln.lab %>" class="btn">Open Lab (<%= vuln.lab %>)</a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
